{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Thank you, Dr. Moreno. Now let me share the manufacturer requirements I confirmed with the distributor today. The manufacturer supplies these hydroxocobalamin kits only in cases of six, requires storage at 2-8 degrees Celsius (refrigerated), and requires a documented staff-use training session to be completed before the first kit can be placed into service. These three requirements will directly impact our decisions on quantity, storage arrangement, and staff readiness. For example, if we stock in the satellite ED, we'll need refrigeration capable of maintaining 2-8 degrees Celsius at that location, and we'll need to plan and document a training session for ED staff before any kits go live. The case-of-six minimum also means our quantity decision should account for that increment."}
